# 💡 Examples

Example flight scripts for the Bumblebee platform, extracted from the drone's system image. Use these as a reference when working on your assignments — the same code runs on the real drone and in the Gazebo simulator.

| Path | What's inside |
| --- | --- |
| `drone.py` | The flight API itself — `takeoff`, `fly_to`, `move`, `hover`, `safe_land`, LEDs, sounds, servo ([full reference](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Drone‐Py‐API)) |
| `flight_profile.py` | Centralized speed/timeout profiles used by drone.py |
| `flight/flight.py` | Minimal full flight: takeoff → hover → precision land |
| `flight/flight_marker.py` | Navigate to an ArUco marker and land on it |
| `flight/flight_marker_loop.py` | Loop over several markers |
| `flight/navigate_wait.py` | Low-level `navigate_wait` usage |
| `flight/example_flight.py` | Multi-waypoint mission |
| `animations/` | LED strip animations (fire, police, rainbow, strobe, …), with their shared helper `_show.py` (keep it next to them). None flashes more than 3 times per second, and they pause while the drone shows a "flight controller lost" or "low battery" alarm. The newer LED/sound shows (party, siren, alarm, victory, rainbow theater) are in `drone/ros2_ws/src/bumblebee/examples/animations/` |
| `misc/` | Small utilities: telemetry, camera, ArUco check, LED, servo, tunes, preflight |

## Running

**In the simulator** (see [Gazebo Setup (Windows)](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Gazebo‐Setup‐(Windows))):

```bash
sim-run flight.py
```

**On the real drone** — copy the script over and run it with Python (the drone is `bumblebee-xxxx.local`, the last 4 hex digits of its Wi-Fi MAC as in its name `Bumblebee-XXXX`, or use its IP):

```bash
scp flight/flight.py lb@bumblebee-xxxx.local:~/
ssh lb@bumblebee-xxxx.local python3 flight.py
```

Full documentation: [Programming Introduction](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Programming‐Introduction) · [Code Examples](https://github.com/futureLabKezad/bumblebee-students/wiki/Code‐Examples)
